column4:
The Prayer For Protection has comforted and reassured millions of people since James Freeman wrote during World War II. Buzz Aldrin had it with him as he made the moonwalk from Apollo 11. It states:
The light of God surrounds us;
The love of God enfolds us;
The power or God protects us;
The presence of God watches over us;
Wherever we are, God is!
We expect that many more people will come to know this prayer initially from the beauty of this plaque. The poem is printed on a glass tile that is three inches wide and six inches tall. It comes with a black, folding metal easel and a gift box.
